note control_nostruct.om: the same bool logic as local_value.om and func_value.om with NO struct:
note bool locals, not, comparison and a bool-returning function. It works with the current
note compiler, so the bool operations are sound and only the struct field is at fault.
note t u a b = true false true false read back as 1 + 2 + 4 + 8 = 15.
fn big x uint to bool
ret gt x 3
end
fn main to uint
x = uint 2
t = lt x 3
u = not t
a = big 5
b = big 2
r = uint 0
if eq t true
r = add r 1
end
if eq u false
r = add r 2
end
if eq a true
r = add r 4
end
if eq b false
r = add r 8
end
ret r
end
